course: dictionary
lesson: 328
title: One word, many animals
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An animal is a living thing that can move and eat. In everyday talk, animal often means a creature like a dog, a bird or a fish. It does not mean a person. «Animals can get trapped in plastic rings by the neck, beak or legs.» Here animals are living things that move about, which is why they can get trapped.
explain: Scientists use animal in a wider way. They sort animals into groups such as mammals, birds, fish, reptiles, amphibians and insects. So in science, an insect is an animal too, even if you would not call it one in everyday talk. Context tells you which meaning the writer wants.
explain: Animal can also be an adjective, a word that describes. «Animal tracks» means tracks made by animals. The word animal does not change its shape here, but its job in the sentence is different. Ask yourself: is animal naming a thing, or describing one?
fact: An animal is a living thing that can move and eat.
fact: In everyday talk, animal often means a mammal or a beast, not a person or an insect.
fact: In science, insects, birds, fish and reptiles are all animals.
fact: «Farm animals», «wild animals», «pet animals» and «animal kingdom» are useful phrases with animal in them.
fact: «Animal tracks» uses animal as an adjective, meaning about animals.
exercise: «Animals can get trapped in plastic rings by the neck, beak or legs.» Which word in this sentence names the living things? | *Animals | Plastic | Rings | Neck
exercise: Ella says a teacher is an animal because she can move and eat. What is wrong with her idea? | Nothing, she is right | Teachers cannot eat, so they cannot be anything | Animals never move | *In everyday talk, animal means a creature like a dog or bird, not a person
exercise: In «animal tracks», what kind of word is animal? | Verb | *Adjective | Adverb | Noun
test: In «A charity is a group that helps people or animals; to donate is to give money to help», what does to donate mean? | To eat a meal | To move from place to place | To hide | *To give money to help
test: Which of these is an animal in everyday talk? | A cloud | A teacher | *A cat | A tree
exam: Which sentence uses animal as an adjective? | The animal ate its lunch | Ben saw a big animal in the field | Animals can get trapped in rings | *Ben found animal tracks in the mud
